    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 1944-10-01; see the referring visit&apos;s Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General</td><td>Alert, warm, and talkative; not sedated; pupils equal and normal in size</td></tr><tr><td>Back</td><td>Lumbar paraspinal tenderness; lumbar bending limited by pain</td></tr><tr><td>Lower limbs</td><td>Right leg thinner and shorter than the left, with weakness and reduced reflexes unchanged from intake; straight-leg raise negative on both sides</td></tr><tr><td>Right ankle and foot</td><td>Bony enlargement and reduced motion; no effusion; foot turned outward</td></tr><tr><td>Gait</td><td>Walks with a cane and a limp from the shorter right leg; rises from a chair using her arms</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
